arity). Channel properties are modulated by cytoplasmic beta subunits that regulate the subcellular location of the alpha subunits and promote rapid inactivation (By similarity). Homotetrameric channels display rapid activation and slow inactivation (PubMed:2347305)"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"},{"commentType":"CATALYTIC ACTIVITY","reaction":{"name":"K(+)(in) = K(+)(out)","reactionCrossReferences":[{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA:29463"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:29103"}],"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"14575698"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"2347305"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"36318112"}]}},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P17659"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}],"value":"Homotetramer and heterotetramer of potassium channel proteins (By similarity). Interacts with KCNAB1 and KCNAB2 (By similarity)"}],"commentType":"SUBUNIT"},{"commentType":"INTERACTION","interactions":[{"interactantOne":{"uniProtKBAccession":"P17658","intActId":"EBI-6426142"},"interactantTwo":{"uniProtKBAccession":"Q99767","geneName":"APBA2","intActId":"EBI-81711"},"numberOfExperiments":2,"organismDiffer":false},{"interactantOne":{"uniProtKBAccession":"P17658","intActId":"EBI-6426142"},"interactantTwo":{"uniProtKBAccession":"Q12959","geneName":"DLG1","intActId":"EBI-357481"},"numberOfExperiments":3,"organismDiffer":false},{"interactantOne":{"uniProtKBAccession":"P17658","intActId":"EBI-6426142"},"interactantTwo":{"uniProtKBAccession":"Q15700","geneName":"DLG2","intActId":"EBI-80426"},"numberOfExperiments":2,"organismDiffer":false},{"interactantOne":{"uniProtKBAccession":"P17658","intActId":"EBI-6426142"},"interactantTwo":{"uniProtKBAccession":"Q92796","geneName":"DLG3","intActId":"EBI-80440"},"numberOfExperiments":3,"organismDiffer":false},{"interactantOne":{"uniProtKBAccession":"P17658","intActId":"EBI-6426142"},"interactantTwo":{"uniProtKBAccession":"Q9UPQ8","