l opening and closing is effected by a conformation change that affects the position and orientation of the voltage-sensor paddle formed by S3 and S4 within the membrane. A transmembrane electric field that is positive inside would push the positively charged S4 segment outwards, thereby opening the pore, while a field that is negative inside would pull the S4 segment inwards and close the pore. Changes in the position and orientation of S4 are then transmitted to the activation gate formed by the inner helix bundle via the S4-S5 linker region"}],"commentType":"DOMAIN"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}],"value":"Belongs to the potassium channel family. A (Shaker) (TC 1.A.1.2) subfamily. Kv1.6/KCNA6 sub-subfamily"}],"commentType":"SIMILARITY"}],"features":[{"type":"Chain","location":{"start":{"value":1,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":529,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Potassium voltage-gated channel subfamily A member 6","featureId":"PRO_0000053990"},{"type":"Topological domain","location":{"start":{"value":1,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":171,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Cytoplasmic","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P63142"}]},{"type":"Transmembrane","location":{"start":{"value":172,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":193,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Helical; Name=Segment S1","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P63142"}]},{"type":"Topological domain","location":{"start":{"value":194,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":262,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Extracellular","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P63142"}]},{"type":"Transmembrane","location":{"start":{"value":263,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":284,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Helical; Name=Segment S2","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P63142"}]},{"type":"Topological domain","location":{"start":{"value":285,"mod